      <h2 id="best-overall-1password">#1 — 1Password (Best Overall Password Manager)</h2>
      <p>1Password ranks as the best overall password manager in 2026 because it combines zero-knowledge encryption with the most polished cross-platform apps in the category. The Secret Key architecture adds a second encryption layer beyond the master password, making 1Password resistant to server-side breaches. Travel Mode, Watchtower breach alerts, and family-shared vaults round out the most complete feature set.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is price and the lack of a permanent free tier. 1Password offers only a 14-day trial, after which individuals pay $2.99/month and families of 5 pay $4.99/month. For users who want free, Bitwarden covers the same core functionality at $0.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>1Password</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Secret Key</strong> — 34-character encryption key in addition to master password</li>
          <li><strong>Travel Mode</strong> — Temporarily remove sensitive vaults when crossing borders</li>
          <li><strong>Watchtower</strong> — Alerts when stored passwords appear in known data breaches</li>
          <li><strong>Family plan</strong> — 5 users, shared vaults for streaming and household accounts</li>
          <li><strong>Cross-platform</strong> — Best-in-class autofill on iOS, Android, macOS, Windows, Linux</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://1password.com" class="btn-alt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Try 1Password Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-free-bitwarden">#2 — Bitwarden (Best Free / Open-Source)</h2>
      <p>Bitwarden is the best free password manager in 2026 because its free tier is genuinely complete — unlimited passwords on unlimited devices, cross-platform sync, browser extensions, and basic two-factor authentication, all with no time limit and no credit card required. The open-source codebase is publicly audited, and the $10/year premium tier adds 2FA token storage and encrypted file attachments.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is interface polish. Bitwarden's apps are functional but less refined than 1Password's, and autofill occasionally requires a second attempt on unusual login forms. For users who prioritize security and free access over a slick UI, these are minor complaints.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>Bitwarden</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Completely free tier</strong> — Unlimited passwords, unlimited devices, no time limit</li>
          <li><strong>Open source &amp; audited</strong> — Code is publicly reviewed by third-party security firms</li>
          <li><strong>AES-256 encryption</strong> — Zero-knowledge architecture, master password never leaves device</li>
          <li><strong>Cross-platform</strong> — Every browser, desktop OS, and mobile platform</li>
          <li><strong>Premium at $10/year</strong> — 2FA tokens, file storage, and priority support</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://bitwarden.com" class="btn-alt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Get Bitwarden Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-premium-dashlane">#3 — Dashlane (Best for Premium Features & VPN)</h2>
      <p>Dashlane is the best password manager for users who want a premium bundle that includes a built-in VPN. The Advanced plan at $4.99/month includes unlimited passwords, dark web monitoring, and a Hotspot Shield-powered VPN. For users who would pay for a VPN separately, Dashlane's bundle delivers combined value that no other password manager matches.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is pricing at the top end. Dashlane's Premium plan at $7.49/month is the most expensive in this list, and the free tier is now limited to 25 passwords on a single device. The VPN is also limited to Wi-Fi protection, not a full-traffic VPN.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>Dashlane</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Built-in VPN</strong> — Hotspot Shield-powered Wi-Fi protection included</li>
          <li><strong>Dark web monitoring</strong> — Alerts when your email or passwords appear in breaches</li>
          <li><strong>Auto-change passwords</strong> — One-click password reset for supported sites</li>
          <li><strong>Secure notes &amp; payments</strong> — Store credit cards, IDs, and encrypted notes</li>
          <li><strong>Free tier</strong> — 25 passwords on 1 device, unlimited password sharing</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://dashlane.com" class="btn-alt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Try Dashlane Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-nord-nordpass">#4 — NordPass (Best for Nord Ecosystem Users)</h2>
      <p>NordPass is the best password manager for users already in the Nord ecosystem (NordVPN, NordLocker). The zero-knowledge architecture uses XChaCha20 encryption instead of AES-256, and the interface is clean and modern. The Premium plan at $1.99/month is one of the most affordable paid options, and bundling with NordVPN delivers additional savings.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is the free tier, which limits to 1 device and requires re-login every 30 days. The app ecosystem is smaller than 1Password or Bitwarden, and the autofill is less reliable on complex login forms.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>NordPass</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>XChaCha20 encryption</strong> — Modern encryption standard, zero-knowledge architecture</li>
          <li><strong>Nord ecosystem</strong> — Bundles with NordVPN and NordLocker for combined savings</li>
          <li><strong>Password health</strong> — Identifies weak, reused, and old passwords</li>
          <li><strong>Autosave &amp; autofill</strong> — Browser extensions and mobile apps</li>
          <li><strong>Free tier</strong> — 1 device, unlimited passwords, 30-day re-login</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://nordpass.com" class="btn-alt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Try NordPass Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-enterprise-keeper">#5 — Keeper (Best for Enterprise & Compliance)</h2>
      <p>Keeper is the best password manager for enterprise teams that need compliance certifications, role-based access control, and audit logging. Keeper holds SOC 2, FedRAMP, HIPAA, and PCI certifications, making it the strongest choice for healthcare, finance, and government contractors. The delegated administration and role-based enforcement policies exceed what 1Password or Bitwarden offer for enterprise.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is consumer UX. Keeper's consumer apps are less polished than 1Password's, and the free tier is limited. The platform is best suited for organizations with IT administrators who manage password policies centrally.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>Keeper</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Compliance certifications</strong> — SOC 2, FedRAMP, HIPAA, PCI, and ISO 27001</li>
          <li><strong>Role-based access</strong> — Delegated administration, team folders, and enforcement policies</li>
          <li><strong>Audit logging</strong> — Full activity logs for compliance and forensics</li>
          <li><strong>KeeperFill</strong> — Browser extension and mobile autofill</li>
          <li><strong>Business plans</strong> — Starting at $3.75/user/month with SSO integration</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://keepersecurity.com" class="btn-alt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Try Keeper Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="selection-scenarios">Selection Scenarios</h2>

      <div class="use-case">
        <h3>Individual / Free Budget</h3>
        <p><strong>Recommendation: Bitwarden Free.</strong> Unlimited passwords on unlimited devices, open-source, audited. There is no better free password manager. Upgrade to $10/year premium only if you need 2FA token storage or encrypted file attachments.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="use-case">
        <h3>Family (2–5 People)</h3>
        <p><strong>Recommendation: 1Password Families at $4.99/month.</strong> Shared vaults for streaming services, household accounts, and emergency access. Travel Mode and Watchtower add security features that Bitwarden's family plan lacks.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="use-case">
        <h3>Enterprise / Regulated Industry</h3>
        <p><strong>Recommendation: Keeper Business.</strong> If your organization needs SOC 2, HIPAA, or FedRAMP compliance, Keeper is the only password manager with all three. For less regulated teams, 1Password Teams or Bitwarden Teams are simpler and cheaper.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="use-case">
        <h3>VPN + Password Manager Bundle</h3>
        <p><strong>Recommendation: Dashlane Advanced.</strong> If you would pay for a VPN separately, Dashlane's bundle at $4.99/month delivers a password manager plus Wi-Fi VPN. NordPass + NordVPN is also a strong bundle for Nord ecosystem users.</p>
      </div>

